---
import Examples from './Examples.astro';
const { example } = Astro.props;
const base = '/raveldex/';
---
<Examples home>
  <section class="search-home__follow" aria-labelledby="build-the-search">
    <div>
      <h2 id="build-the-search">Make it your own</h2>
      <div class="search-home__links">
        <a href={base + 'examples/inline/'}>Get the inline starter <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a href={base + 'guide/overview/'}>Getting started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="search-home__code">
      <figcaption>JavaScript · From an initialized engine</figcaption>
      <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Search code example"><code><span class="search-home__keyword">const</span> result = <span class="search-home__keyword">await</span> engine.search(<span class="search-home__string">'module worker'</span>);</code></pre>
    </figure>
  </section>
  <section class="search-home__example site-main--article" aria-labelledby="a-small-working-example">
    <h2 id="a-small-working-example">A small working example</h2>
    <p>After <a href={base + 'guide/overview/#install-the-package'}>installing core</a>, save this as <code>search.mjs</code> and run <code>node search.mjs</code>. It adds one document and searches for <code>atomic</code>.</p>
    <details><summary>View the complete core example</summary><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Complete core example"><code>{example}</code></pre></details>
    <p>You should see revision <code>1</code>, a total of <code>1</code> and one hit with ID <code>guide:updates</code>. Look up that ID in your application to get its title and URL. The example disposes the engine when it finishes.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="search-home__tasks site-main--article" aria-labelledby="what-would-you-like-to-build">
    <h2 id="what-would-you-like-to-build">What would you like to build?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={base + 'reference/core/'}>Add records, search and update a collection</a>.</li>
      <li><a href={base + 'reference/hosts/#native-dom-ui-and-css'}>Mount a browser search form and style it</a>.</li>
      <li><a href={base + 'reference/addons/'}>Add phrases, filters, facets and snippets</a>.</li>
      <li><a href={base + 'reference/hosts/#one-owner-module-worker'}>Run a module worker</a> or <a href={base + 'reference/hosts/#source-and-native-snapshots'}>save source snapshots</a>.</li>
      <li><a href={base + 'reference/static-astro/'}>Add search to Astro pages</a> with the <a href={base + 'examples/astro/'}>setup/build/preview example</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Read the <a href={base + 'guide/compatibility/'}>runtime requirements</a> and <a href={base + 'guide/limitations/'}>practical limits</a> before choosing optional capabilities.</p>
  </section>
</Examples>
